# A span is offsets, on character boundaries, and covers exactly what was
# found (the runner holds every case of every file to that). The texts with
# a value shaped like a real key are built in `spans.rs`.

# An escape that is not printable ASCII is left alone: a line end, a control
# character and a letter that is not ASCII.
rules=generic_secret span="fake%0APass0word1" | password=fake%0APass0word1
rules=generic_secret span="\\u00e9FakeToken01" | token=\\u00e9FakeToken01
rules=generic_secret span="fake&#10;ApiKey01" | api_key=fake&#10;ApiKey01
safe | see %41KIA and \\u0041KI and &#65K

# A percent-encoded query is read, and the span is the value as written.
span="fake%50ass0word1" | https://x.io/?q=password%3Dfake%50ass0word1&x=1
span="alice%2Esmith%40acme.io" | https://x.io/?mail=alice%2Esmith%40acme.io
